course: dictionary
lesson: 8912
title: Siblings: brothers and sisters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sibling is a brother or sister. Siblings is the plural, so two or more brothers and sisters are siblings. «Ella has 3 siblings» means Ella has 3 brothers and/or sisters, and she does not count herself.
explain: Context words tell you more about the siblings. «Step-siblings at the same school may act differently there than at home» shows they are joined through a parent's marriage. Words such as older, younger, half, step and twin show what kind of sibling someone is.
explain: Some phrases use the word too. An «only child» has no siblings. «Sibling rivalry» means brothers and sisters competing or arguing, which is normal. Sharing, taking turns and talking it out help, as the sentence «ask siblings calmly to knock» suggests.
fact: A sibling is a brother or sister.
fact: Siblings is the plural word for more than one brother or sister.
fact: Half-siblings share one parent; step-siblings are joined through a parent's marriage.
fact: Twins are siblings born at the same time.
fact: Sibling rivalry means brothers and sisters competing or arguing, and it is normal.
exercise: «Hard times can bring siblings closer.» What is a sibling? | A parent | A cousin who lives far away | *A brother or sister | A teacher
exercise: Ella has 3 siblings. How many brothers and sisters does Ella have, not counting herself? | 1 | 2 | *3 | 4
exercise: Sam and Ruby keep arguing about the TV every evening. Which phrase describes this? | Step-parent | Young carer | Only child | *Sibling rivalry
test: «Step-siblings are joined through a parent's marriage.» Which word means a child with no brothers or sisters? | Twin | Young carer | Half-sibling | *Only child
test: Which siblings share one parent? | Only children | *Half-siblings | Twins | Step-siblings
exam: «When a baby is ill, older siblings feel the worry too.» Which word in this sentence means brothers and sisters? | older | baby | worry | *siblings
